{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"01a08098-c0e5-7700-b7a3-923d69d1d67d","outcome":{"verdict":"needs-fix","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/publish-at-job-boundaries/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"reason":"レビュー証拠レポートを review-feedback-001.md に書き出しました。HIGH 2件、MEDIUM 1件を報告しています。","approved":false,"findings":[{"severity":"high","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/step/commit-push.ts","title":"Terminal commit failure can be reported as successful publication","rationale":"commitFinalState warns and returns when the checkpoint/final-state commit fails. The caller then publishes the previous HEAD and may receive published or already-synchronized, allowing completion or remote-ready guidance even though the final records were never committed.","line":899,"origin":"scope","remediation":{"invariant":"A terminal boundary must not report successful publication unless its required final/checkpoint records were committed and published.","sites":[{"file":"src/core/step/commit-push.ts","line":899},{"file":"src/core/pipeline/pipeline.ts","line":426},{"file":"src/core/command/runner.ts","line":352}],"approach":"Return a typed commit result, distinguish no-change from commit failure, and suppress successful completion or remote-ready guidance on failure while preserving local retry state."}},{"severity":"high","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/pipeline/pipeline.ts","title":"Pre-PR publication failure loses its phase-specific error type","rationale":"The pre-PR publisher throws PUBLICATION_FAILED, but the surrounding executor catch converts exceptions without an attached state into UNEXPECTED_STEP_ERROR. Persistent state therefore loses the required pre-PR publication phase and retry diagnosis, although the PR API remains uncalled.","line":297,"origin":"scope","remediation":{"invariant":"Pre-PR push, PR API, and post-PR push failures must remain distinguishable in persisted state and CLI diagnostics.","sites":[{"file":"src/core/pipeline/pipeline.ts","line":297},{"file":"src/core/pipeline/pipeline.ts","line":304}],"approach":"Move pre-PR publication outside the executor catch or preserve SpecRunnerError code and phase details explicitly; add a persistence-level regression test."}},{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/pipeline/pipeline.ts","title":"Disabling halt publication also disables the local checkpoint commit","rationale":"The policy conditional wraps commitFinalState as well as publication. With publishCheckpointOnHalt=false, controlled halts persist files but do not create the scoped local checkpoint commit required before the conditional publication decision. The pre-pipeline fidelity gate has the same issue.","line":657,"origin":"scope","remediation":{"invariant":"Every controlled halt must persist and locally commit its safe checkpoint; only remote publication is policy-controlled.","sites":[{"file":"src/core/pipeline/pipeline.ts","line":657},{"file":"src/core/command/runner.ts","line":351}],"approach":"Always run scoped commitFinalState after halt persistence, then guard only publishCommittedState with the stored policy; test both pipeline and gate halt paths."}}],"evidence":{"checked":18,"skipped":4,"unverified":14},"fixableCount":3},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0},"startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:38:08.925Z","endedAt":"2026-09-08T10:42:16.643Z","commitOid":"7fbc7f94d2e2c2677b7e7a0e7c8d61ac9b089be8"}
